Known bugs
=-=-=-=-==
This is a list of known bugs in SMSQ/E.


1 - (all versions)
If the FIRST variable enumerated when an SBASIC daughter job is parsed, is
used as a formal parameter in a function/procedure, the machine will
crash badly. This does not happens in job 0.

According to Per Witte, this description was formulated by Martyn Hill.

Example program showing the bug:

100 p$ = 'abc': p = 123
110 :
120 test p$, p
130 PAUSE
140 :
150 DEFine PROCedure test(p$, p)
160   PRINT "It doesn't get here"
170 END DEFine test

Workarounds:

A
Initiate another variable first:
100 dummy = 0: p$ = 'abc': p = 123

 (rest unchanged)

B
Replace this line
150 DEFine PROCedure test(p$, p)
with
150 DEFine PROCedure test(another_name$, p)
i.e. do not use "p$" as formal parameter in the procedure definition

 (rest unchanged)
